# Plan-orchestrate protocol

Use this rule when work benefits from multiple bounded phases. A named provider
or model is never mandatory. Route by capability, risk, availability, and cost
using `.exocortex/control/MODEL_ROUTING.md`.

1. Keep one accountable parent for planning, integration, and gate decisions.
2. Choose the least-expensive available parent that can safely own the full
   task. Escalate when evidence shows the selected tier is insufficient.
3. Delegate narrow, read-only or deterministic evidence gathering to cheaper
   capable workers. Use one guarded writer for mutations.
4. Give every worker a compact context packet: work item, exact revision and
   base, role, allowed paths, acceptance criteria, authority, and stop rules.
5. Verify each result deterministically where possible. Independent review is
   required only when the work item's gate or risk classification requires it.
6. Treat a phase stop as a reminder to consider a local narrative save. It is
   not an automatic save, lifecycle transition, checkpoint, approval, commit,
   deployment, or external synchronization.

Model discovery is proposal-only. Route from fresh, digest-bound
official-source, current-surface availability, and measured evaluation
evidence; quarantine newly observed models and fail closed on stale,
unavailable, or mismatched evidence.

Narrative saves are local project memory. Lifecycle checkpoints are created
only by an accepted, authorized, durable transition marked checkpoint-eligible.
External sync always uses a separate exact destination-specific authorization.
